      "message": "This class encapsulates only couple of `public` methods and has no data members or private methods. If the intention is to avoid namespace collisions, can we wrap these methods in a `namespace` instead of a `class` ?\n\nA `class` has overhead attached with it. To use any of the class methods, we would need to create an object of the class, whereas a `namespace` is the most memory-efficient option because it guarantees zero overhead.",
